WEBVTT

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>Ready... 1, 2, 3, GO!</i>

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.160
<i>Love life! Very! Very! Happy!</i>

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.950
<i>Friendship life! Bouncing, jumping!</i>

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.660
<i>Adventure life! Heart-pounding, OK?</i>

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.620
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:28.260
<i>Rushing out onto the road to</i>
<i>school with the blue sky behind us</i>

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.220
<i>I like that! I like this, too!</i>

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.720
<i>I'll take it all, all of it~</i>

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.600
<i>A girl who imagines love is all romance</i>

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>If I can attack, I'll do it boldly</i>

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.980
<i>Let's find an original vision for the future</i>

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:49.900
<i>Sometimes, we'll have a secret love advice time</i>

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.740
<i>Who do you like?</i>

00:00:52.950 --> 00:01:00.290
<i>You've got a green light for love now!</i>
<i>It's your chance to move forward!</i>

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.120
<i>So, let's just</i>

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:04.120
<i>Have a blast! Fall in love!</i>

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.210
<i>Our youth is non-stop!</i>

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.300
<i>Run! Aim for the future!</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.920
<i>Everyone gather</i>

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.800
<i>For a happy ending!</i>

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:15.340
<i>Will tomorrow be happy or sad?</i>
<i>Will we idle our time away?</i>

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.430
<i>We'll work hard!</i>

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.720
<i>I want to keep dreaming forever!</i>

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.940
<i>Let's fly out into the</i>
<i>world with all our strength!</i>

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.820
<i>Song of youth! Come on ready? Let's go!</i>

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:41.830
An ant killing an elephant is an apt phrase.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.540
For this godlike black monster to be
worried about a small ant-like pebble

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.000
that entered his shoe...

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.010
In addition, as if rubbing salt into the wound,

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:05.060
this unruly long hair is pointing
at the sky in an unthinkable direction.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.400
This is the worst.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.990
Dark monsters may take advantage
of the darkness in people's hearts.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.620
Darkness in their hearts?

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:23.080
What do you mean?

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.250
Oh, you know. In Yokai Street,
there was someone who turned into a monster...

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.250
Little Tsugihagi, I think?

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:32.210
It's only natural to come to that
conclusion based on that incident, right?

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.510
I'm sure this is also Dagger's doing, darling!

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.760
I see. We need to be careful, too.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:47.270
But Mr. Berry, you've turned
completely feminine, haven't you...?

00:02:55.570 --> 00:03:01.070
It looks like all that's left is to practice
to make this song completely ours.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.250
Hey, Mr. Berry, what did you think?

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:09.960
Huh?

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.540
Is he sleeping, pyuru?

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:16.460
For a little while now, there have been
times when it seems like his spirit is gone.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:19.470
Recently, he's been gone more often than not.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.340
That's strange, pyuru.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:28.140
In any case, being able to perform in the
Grateful Rock Festival is like a dream come true.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:31.020
But if we don't leave our mark here...

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.360
Terrible news!

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:40.280
Well? What's so terrible?

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:46.450
Well, at this rate, Plasmagica won't
be able to perform in the festival.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.960
Why not?

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.710
When I sent in this application form

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:55.130
with a demo tape of the song
you'd perform, "Ryuusei Dreamline,"

00:03:55.340 --> 00:04:00.380
the song thankfully passed, but this—! This—!

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:03.220
The "Live Point"?

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:05.470
There was a requirement like that?

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.560
It's true that we haven't had
a proper live concert yet.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.940
Does that mean we can't perform?

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.860
Oh, don't tell me Shingan can't, either?

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:18.740
No, they were the opening
band for Trichronika before.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.860
That counted, so they passed easily.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.160
It's not something we're proud of, though.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:30.210
Oi, you guys! How long are you
gonna drag out your practice?

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:35.170
My Red Tomahawk is waiting
anxiously for a chance to come out!

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.210
Oh! Sorry...

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.920
Even if you say that, you're not all here yet.

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.130
What?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.720
It's true. I do not see Aion in this training room.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.100
You didn't notice till now?

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:51.020
What's that Aion dragging his feet for?

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.350
He'll probably just say—

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.560
"The sun god of darkness has
low blood pressure, so it couldn't be helped."

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.480
—again or something.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.530
If he says something that sounds that much
like an office worker's excuse for being late,

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.110
I won't let him off easy!

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.320
Anyway, let's think of a way around this.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:10.330
After we've come this far, it's unthinkable
for us to not perform in the festival!

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.670
Let's do anything we have to to participate!

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.580
I have an idea about that.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:19.210
I'll tell you more in the café.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:36.730
Actually, I was wondering what you thought
about doing another battle of the bands!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.070
Battle of the bands? With whom?

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.320
Don't tell me you want us
to play against Criticrista again?

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.160
As expected of Chuchu.
You're quick to understand.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.370
But Cri-Cri is on a roll right now, pyuru!

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:52.040
What if we lose again, pyuru?

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:55.330
But right now, it's not an
issue of whether we win or lose.

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:58.590
Isn't it just important for us to perform
a concert at the battle of the bands?

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:03.760
With that song, we have a
chance of beating Criticrista.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:08.550
If we win this and bring
that momentum to the festival,

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.220
we'd definitely be the number one band to watch!

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:15.230
That might be true, but let's not
get too worked up about that.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.730
Yes, you're right.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:21.730
But will they accept our rematch?

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:25.320
That's where I'll show you my power.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:33.700
Right now, I'll... call... Ogasawara...!

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:42.840
Hello? This is Banded Rocking Records.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:48.390
Yes. Right, I am calling to ask
for a battle of the bands rematch.

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:51.050
Yes. Is that right?

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.310
We look forward to working with you again.

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.600
They readily gave their okay.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:58.810
Plas...

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:00.230
...magica...

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:05.570
However, their schedule is pretty full,
so it has to be next weekend.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:06.440
Next week?!

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.530
We barely have any time!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.030
Now that it's been decided,
we have to practice! Practice!

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.950
But right now Shingan
is using the studio, pyuru...

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.330
Oh, that's right...

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.040
Well, why don't we call it a day?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:25.590
Yes, let's take a break.

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:26.420
Yeah!

00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:28.130
It's time for snacks!

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.010
Snacks are good for the soul!

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.300
So what are we having today?

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:35.970
Cream puffs.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.520
Wait!

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:46.780
Hello, ladies of Criticrista.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.450
Dagger, sir!

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:52.910
Plasmagica just said they wanted
to have another battle of the bands.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:57.040
I accepted, but will you do it?

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.080
Yes! It's what we wanted!

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.960
Oh? That's good to hear.

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.250
Rosia forgot to act cute.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.340
I wonder what's wrong...?

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.880
She's serious about this.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:15.560
This time, we'll definitely beat them to a pulp
so they won't be able to stand up again!

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:20.100
I see. Even so, the enemy is pretty strong.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.060
Can you win so easily against Cyan?

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.280
Hey, Plasmagica wants
to challenge you girls again.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:34.820
We know already!

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.620
Yes, ma'am...

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:44.420
Ah, I can't wait anymore!

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:49.260
The flow of time is limited and cannot
be changed at one's discretion.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:52.630
If humans are small, weak beings,

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:56.760
then we have no choice but
to treasure each second we have. Hence—

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.970
Let's hurry up and start practice.

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:01.310
It can't be helped.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:16.240
Oi, Aion! You're so late that the strings of
my dear Red Tomahawk were about to rust!

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.120
Hey, hurry up and get ready, Aion!

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:23.330
For you to be this late, were you involved
in some kind of Legend of Accident?

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.750
- Hence—
- Hey, are you listening?!

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.960
It's fine. Just hurry up and get ready!

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:34.720
Oh right, about that new song you arranged.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:37.260
The order is all over the place,
and we're having a hard time with it.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.930
Will you think about those
of us performing it, too?

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:47.360
It's hard having to save your lame,
weak songs with my lyrics time after tim—

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:51.530
You... That tuft of hair...

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.740
D-Don't make me laugh!

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.240
"Lame, weak songs," huh?

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:05.620
You're right. It's not like the
songs I write are any good...

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:09.420
Aion... you're not posing...

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.720
I hate anything and everything!

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:17.050
I quit...!

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:31.070
I knew it! You're still
not practicing yet, pyuru!

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.820
Then, will you let us use the studio?

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.870
Did something happen?

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:47.870
It's because you called Aion's songs lame!

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:51.250
And then you laughed at his bed head!
What are you, a kid?!

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:52.800
Huh?! It's <i>my</i> fault?

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.760
Yeah! It's your fault!

00:10:56.130 --> 00:11:00.350
No, this isn't the first time Crow
has said those things. Hence—

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:09.980
Is that right? That always-gloomy Aion
was 1.6 times gloomier than usual?

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:12.110
That barely makes sense.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:16.320
Hey, do you remember what happened
with Tsugihagi from Shinimonogurui?

00:11:20.950 --> 00:11:29.080
Mr. Berry said maybe dark monsters took
advantage of the darkness in Myumons' hearts.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.380
Which means—

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.460
I'm worried about Aion, pyuru.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:35.250
Shouldn't you find him as soon as possible?

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:36.420
You're right.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.170
I agree. Hence—

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.800
I'm not going!

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:42.100
Crow, you...

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.640
Are you not concerned about Aion?

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:49.890
The words "I quit" are absolutely taboo!

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:53.980
That bastard. He said them so easily.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:57.110
He can do what he wants! Hmph!

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:03.030
Fine. Anyway, we'll look for him for now.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.370
We should help look, too!

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:06.410
Yes.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:08.450
It'll be better if we all
searched together, right?

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.000
Pyuru!

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:12.040
Yeah, thanks.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:18.420
That guy might come back here.
If that happens, you should keep him here.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.220
Like I care.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.260
Well, we'll be back.

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.730
Where Aion would go?

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.940
Yeah, is there anywhere you can think of?

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:43.870
Well, stores related
to music seem the most likely.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:45.320
Anywhere else?

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:49.750
For now, all we can do is
search everywhere we can think of.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.760
That was a great concert, Shu☆zo!

00:13:03.890 --> 00:13:09.350
I think you twins did well
working hard to make me shine!

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:10.770
Really?

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.690
Thank you!

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:15.400
Oh?

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:18.520
Shu☆zo, isn't the person standing over there

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:22.570
a member of the band
that opened for us the other day?

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:30.620
What's he doing in a place like that?

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:34.120
He seems to be surrounded
by a really negative aura...

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:43.720
He's a shut-in with a communication
disorder and can't talk unless he poses.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:47.140
But you could probably say that
he has the most musical talent

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.680
and the most love for music in our band.

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:56.520
That's why I never thought I'd ever
hear him say he was quitting the band.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:57.690
Hence—

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:00.150
Yeah, and that Crow.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:07.160
He's always saying mean things, but he's the
one who recognizes Aion's talent the most.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:10.330
The songs with soul that Aion writes,

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:14.250
and the lyrics filled with soul
that Crow throws at them...

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:19.670
They become our passionate
crimson songs and are refined...

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.590
So to lose Aion...

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.300
It's unthinkable!

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.510
Rom...

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:33.020
I don't want to watch a friend leave...

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.100
...ever again!

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:44.190
This is... Trichronika's vehicle...

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:52.870
Hey, Rom!

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:54.080
Hence...

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:55.870
We meet again!

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.750
What do you want, Shu?

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.040
We're busy here.

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:04.460
You're the only one
who calls me by that name now.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:12.390
Anyway, if you're looking for a guitarist
being eaten away by a squirming dark aura,

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:13.890
I know where he is.

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:14.560
What?

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:16.520
It's none of your business!
I don't need you to—

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:21.020
Isn't he your precious bandmate?

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.690
Unless...

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:26.110
...you wish misfortune to befall <i>another</i> friend.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.240
You bastard...

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.620
Try going to the Shibu Valley Center Building!

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:39.330
See ya!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:44.340
Rom!

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:46.630
R-R-Right.

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:55.100
What's wrong, you two?

00:15:56.770 --> 00:15:59.440
Is something bothering you?

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:00.600
Um...

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:01.850
Well...

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.860
About that drummer named Rom earlier...

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:07.860
Do you know him?

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:13.450
You seemed to know each other from way back...

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.830
Once, there were friends who shared a dream.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:22.830
The goal of one was to make
his own dream come true,

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:25.630
and he valued that above everything.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:31.130
However, the other wished
for blessings through that dream.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:34.720
In time, even though they should have
been chasing the same dream,

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.850
they could not walk together anymore,

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:40.520
and went their separate ways.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.240
I'll bring him back even if I have
to put a rope around his neck.

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:00.080
That was my intention from the start, as well.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:02.040
Hey, Aion!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.960
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:12.260
This god has already left SHINGANCRIMSONZ.

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:16.220
What I do here by myself
is none of your business.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.760
Aion, bastard!

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:30.530
Don't spout nonsense about leaving on your own!

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:34.700
Someone like me...

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:36.030
Huh?

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:39.040
Even if someone like me weren't there...

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.040
Are you still saying that, bastard?!

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:41.950
Rom!

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:44.330
You idiot!

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:49.590
Crow...

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:59.010
I can't allow you to leave us,

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:03.390
but more than that,
I can't allow you to make this guy sad.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.270
He was crying, you know...

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:23.830
Listen, Aion! You haven't
left SHINGANCRIMSONZ yet!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.120
No one has accepted your resignation yet!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:34.510
And, well... maybe... I said too much, too...

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.680
But don't say annoying things like "I quit"!

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.720
I'll only say this once!

00:18:44.270 --> 00:18:51.940
I will never allow a band member
who wrote such soulful songs to leave!

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:57.240
We're able to live passionately
because of your songs!

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:20.050
This god made the mistake of a lifetime.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:25.770
I can't believe this
under-sized rodent saved my soul.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.270
Oh, shut up.

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.440
My eyes... Are these tears...?

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:36.990
I thought they had dried up long ago...

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:50.420
Through fire or water,
if the four of us are together,

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:53.090
we can overcome any trouble!

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:57.720
Even if a huge wall blocks our way,

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:01.800
one day, the four of us will break through it!

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:11.100
That's right. We're—

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:13.730
SHINGANCRIMSONZ!

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:18.360
What? You found him?

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.450
Oh good, pyuru!

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:24.450
Hello, everyone!

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:28.790
I'm Rosia, from Criticrista!

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:33.130
We're going to be in
another battle of the bands!

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:37.130
We'll be battling a band
we played against before, Plasmagica.

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:40.220
Are you watching, Cyan?

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.510
Huh?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:46.100
This time, I'll flatten you for sure!

00:20:46.310 --> 00:20:47.470
Just kidding!

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:51.560
Everyone, we're counting on your support!

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:01.490
It's finally time for the Grateful Rock Festival!

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.160
There'll sure be a ton of popular bands there!

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:06.160
I wanna go to Midi City...

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:07.830
I wanna go watch...

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:09.580
You've gotta fight to get tickets!

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:11.160
What about online auctions?

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:15.880
They're real expensive.
High schoolers like us don't have a chance...

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:19.380
Speaking of Cri-Cri,
they're doing another battle of the bands.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:21.470
Against what band?

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:24.720
Plasmagica or something, I think?

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:26.680
Who's that?

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:29.930
Sorry! Math is the pits!

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:32.020
Huh? What's wrong, guys?

00:21:32.230 --> 00:21:34.520
- I wanna go to Midi City!
- I wanna go to Midi City!

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:36.400
Oh, Midi City's great!

00:21:36.610 --> 00:21:39.570
If we go, we have to go
there to buy clothes first!

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:41.610
Huh? You're starting from that?

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:43.650
Who's Plasma?

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:46.410
Anyway, what're we gonna do
about the school festival?

00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:49.990
Oh, don't drag me back to reality...!

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:53.080
I said, who's Plasma?!

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:03.050
<i>If you like it, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:05.930
<i>You can do it because you like it</i>

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:08.640
<i>The feeling that you like music</i>

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:12.020
<i>Can't be stopped by anyone</i>

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:20.440
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:22.650
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:26.200
<i>Running through my body</i>

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:28.740
<i>This electric thrill</i>

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:33.750
<i>Is this feeling curiosity?</i>

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:37.290
<i>Negativity is a decrescendo</i>

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:39.960
<i>Hope and expectations, a crescendo</i>

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:45.510
<i>Show off our passion and</i>
<i>get god to be our ally, too</i>

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:51.010
<i>I wanna share with everyone and have a taste of</i>

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:54.730
<i>Big!! Rocking!! Heart-throbbing!! Happiness!!!!</i>

00:22:55.730 --> 00:22:58.770
<i>If it's you, I'm sure you can do it</i>

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:01.770
<i>You can do it because it's you</i>

00:23:01.980 --> 00:23:06.860
<i>Let's try performing these</i>
<i>dream-colored notes together</i>

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:10.070
<i>I want to tell you directly</i>

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:12.910
<i>A life-sized, "heart-sized" heart</i>

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:15.790
<i>In order for it to reach you...</i>

00:23:16.000 --> 00:23:19.120
<i>I will sing with all I have</i>

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.880
<i>GO GO LUCKY Have a nice MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:23.840
<i>GO GO HAPPY MUSIC!!</i>

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:27.510
Now, today we have Rosia from Cri-Cri.

00:23:27.720 --> 00:23:28.760
Let's cut to the chase. What's your hobby?

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:30.680
Um, shopping!

00:23:30.890 --> 00:23:33.930
I love trying on cute clothes,
looking at myself in the mirror,

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:36.350
and having the clerk say,
"That looks good on you."

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:37.520
I love it!

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:39.690
Love, huh...?
